Z||000004||grinthock||11-01-2001||07:47 PM||||I am running XP Corporate.<BR> <BR>My 2000 Professional refused to upgrade for some reason.  <P>My opinion?  Don't go XP.  Wait till service pack 1 comes out for it AT LEAST.  We all know it will.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Robert||11-01-2001||08:07 PM||||Thanks all<BR>We have already reinstalled win98 on the puter at the shop.  We had to FDISK the puter in order to reinstall win98; even though the XP instructions say there is no problem going back to your old system.  We to are sure there will be upgrades coming out REAL soon.  This installation is so user un-friendly, Microsoft is going to be hearing a lot about it.  Funny thing is, nowhere in the instruction is a help phone number.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||grinthock||11-01-2001||09:13 PM||||You couldn't go back because you picked the option to convert your drive to NTFS, which is New Technology File System, which is not compatible with Win98.  What they DO NOT tell you during the install/upgrade is that if you decide to convert it (as recommended) you can not just migrate back.||||reg||1
