Z||000009||fieronv||11-02-2001||04:13 PM||||When I installed xp pro over win2k it ran for a week and then crashed hard enough that I had to format the hard drive and do a clean install. I then read that it is not a good idea to over write a previous os. I have now been running xp for 6 weeks with no problems but I'm going to wait to do my home machine for a few months or until they come out with a service pack.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||11-02-2001||09:48 PM||||Microsoft <I>always</I> says that you can upgrade from a previous version. By the time you find out that you really can't, you've already plunked down your money. Gotcha!<BR>The only time I've done an upgrade was from 95 to 98. Seemed to work okay, though.<BR>Others were a fresh install. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT>||||reg||1
